<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Putprop half yr share rises, declares div.</title>
<headline>Putprop half yr share rises, declares div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     16.3     vs    15.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  7.0     vs     --</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    7.29    vs     6.18</p>
<p>    Tax			  2.58    vs     1.87</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    3.18    vs     3.67</p>
<p>    Interest received	0.71    vs     0.69</p>
<p>    Gross rentals	   10.15    vs     9.42</p>
<p>Div payable: April 18</p>
<p>On register: April 4</p>
<p>Full name: Putco Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that during 1997, rentals would increase by about 1.6 million rand. This was slightly below the forecast of 1.8 million rand in the chairman's statement in the 1996 annual report. However, an increase in interest received would more than compensate for the shortfall. In the longer term the outlook for the group remained favourable, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
